428	// An end node's result is delivered to the caller verbatim for primitives
429	// (null, undefined, strings, numbers, booleans), but an object or array result
430	// must be structured-clonable: the engine snapshots it independently both at
431	// validation time and again when the end node actually runs. A function (or a
432	// symbol, getter-built object the clone algorithm rejects, etc.) nested in a
433	// result object/array is a definition error naming the end node and reason;
434	// bare function results cannot be delivered through JSON-style results either.
435	//
436	// Cloneability alone is not enough: structured cloning a SharedArrayBuffer (or
437	// a typed array / DataView backed by one) "succeeds" while the clone keeps
438	// sharing the underlying bytes with the definition's result, so the caller
439	// could rewrite the returned bytes and silently change the definition and
440	// every later run — the promised independent copy could not be delivered.
441	// As with legacy messages, run inputs and operation returns, the clone is
442	// therefore produced first and judged with containsSharedMemory: only shared
443	// memory the clone actually retains condemns the result (an attached property
444	// of a Date/RegExp, a non-enumerable or symbol-keyed property, an Error own
445	// property other than cause are discarded by the clone and never inspected).
